L1: October 14 2026; National Geodetic Survey Remote Sensing Division.
L3: Light Detection and Ranging (LIDAR) is a subject studied by the NGS Remote Sensing Research and Development Team.
L4: LIDAR is an active remote sensing system, operated in profiling or scanning mode using light pulses to illuminate terrain. Airborne collection combines a laser scanner, kinematic GPS to locate x,y,z, and inertial navigation to monitor pitch, roll and heading.
L5: Measuring round-trip travel time of a laser pulse from aircraft to ground allows a spot elevation to be calculated.
L6-L9: NGS has tested applications including beach damage, Greenland ice sheet, forest heights, shoreline definition, and point data.
L10-L14: Navigation/footer and last modified 16 May 2017.

